## Layout

```
src/{{ package_name }}/
  main.py            application factory and lifespan
  api/router.py      where routes are mounted
  api/routes/        one module per resource
  core/config.py     settings, read from the environment
  core/logging.py    text logs locally, JSON in production
{% if uses_database %}
  db/session.py      engine + one transaction per request
  db/base.py         declarative base and naming conventions
  models/            SQLAlchemy models
  schemas/           request and response models
migrations/          Alembic
{% endif %}
tests/
```

## Quickstart

```bash
make install
{% if uses_database and database == "postgres" %}
cp .env.example .env
{% if has_addon('docker') %}
make up            # API + Postgres in Docker
{% else %}
# point {{ env_prefix }}DATABASE_URL at a running Postgres, then:
