make run
{% endif %}
{% else %}
cp .env.example .env
make run
{% endif %}
make test
```

- API: http://localhost:8000
- Docs: http://localhost:8000/docs
- Health: http://localhost:8000/health/live and `/health/ready`

## Configuration

Every setting is an environment variable prefixed `{{ env_prefix }}`, or a line
in `.env` for local development. See `.env.example` and
`src/{{ package_name }}/core/config.py`.

| Variable | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `{{ env_prefix }}ENVIRONMENT` | `local` | `local`, `test`, `staging`, `production` |
| `{{ env_prefix }}LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | JSON logs once environment is `production` |
| `{{ env_prefix }}CORS_ORIGINS` | `["http://localhost:5173"]` | JSON list |
{% if uses_database %}
| `{{ env_prefix }}DATABASE_URL` | see `.env.example` | async driver required |
{% endif %}
{% if uses_database %}

## Migrations

```bash
make revision m="add users table"   # autogenerate from the models
make migrate                        # apply
make downgrade                      # roll back one
```

A model is only visible to autogenerate if it is imported in
`src/{{ package_name }}/models/__init__.py`.
{% endif %}

